= Water Cycle: Grade 4 Lesson Plan

_Duration: 45 minutes_

== Learning Objectives

By the end of the lesson, students will be able to:

- Name the four main stages of the water cycle: evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and collection.
- Explain in their own words how water moves between the ground, the air, and back again.
- Describe the role of the sun as the energy source that drives the cycle.

== Materials

- Clear zip-top bags (one per pair of students)
- Permanent marker and masking tape
- Warm water (about 50 mL per bag)
- Small cup of ice cubes or cold water
- Sunny window or lamp for each group
- Projector or whiteboard with a simple water cycle diagram
- Printed exit ticket (one per student)
- Vocabulary cards: evaporation, condensation, precipitation, collection, water vapor, cloud

